<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <%- include('partials/header') %>
    <style>
        .privacy-notice {
            max-width: 760px;
            margin: 1.5rem auto 3rem;
            padding: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
            background: var(--bg-card);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
            box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
            line-height: 1.65;
        }
        .privacy-notice h2 { margin-top: 1.75rem; }
        .privacy-notice a { color: var(--blue-link); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <div class="container px-3">
        <main class="privacy-notice">
            <h1 class="t-h1">Privacy Notice</h1>
            <p class="t-small">Last updated: September 15, 2026</p>
            <p>Bracket 10 is a friendly basketball picks game operated from Virginia. This notice explains
                how we use information when you visit, enter, or manage your picks.</p>

            <h2 class="t-h2">What we collect and why</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Your entry:</strong> your name, team name, email address, group, team selections,
                    and entry records. We use these to run the game, calculate standings, and help you manage your entry.</li>
                <li><strong>Google sign-in:</strong> if you choose it, Google provides basic profile information
                    and a verified email address. We use your email to find your entries and keep you signed in.
                    We do not receive your Google password.</li>
                <li><strong>Technical information:</strong> our hosting and security services process information
                    such as IP addresses, browser details, and requests to operate the site, diagnose errors,
                    and prevent abuse.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="t-h2">What other people can see</h2>
            <p>Your name, team name, picks, scores, and standings can be viewed on group results and bracket pages,
                including past tournaments. These pages are not restricted to signed-in players. Choose names
                you are comfortable sharing. Your email is not displayed on public results or bracket pages;
                site administrators can access it to manage your entry.</p>

            <h2 class="t-h2">How we use your email</h2>
            <p>We use your email to confirm your signup, provide access to your entry, and help you change your
                team selections. We also use it to verify entry ownership. We do not use addresses collected
                through the site for marketing, newsletters, or future-season invitations.</p>

            <h2 class="t-h2">Services that help us run the game</h2>
            <p>We use Google Cloud to host the site and store game information, and Google for optional sign-in.
                Email services and tools used to prepare entry emails, including AI-assisted drafting tools,
                may process your email address and entry details for that purpose. Site assets also load from
                third-party providers, which receive connection information such as your IP address.</p>
            <p>We do not sell your personal information. We may disclose information when required by law or
                when necessary to address misuse or protect the site and its players.</p>

            <h2 class="t-h2">Cookies, browser storage, and analytics</h2>
            <p>We use a session cookie to remember sign-in and entry verification. Browser storage remembers
                preferences such as your color theme and caches site resources. You can clear these through
                your browser settings; doing so may sign you out or reset preferences.</p>
            <p>This site uses Google Analytics to understand visits and site usage. It uses cookies and
                collects information about your browser, device, and activity on the site. Learn more about
                <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>
                and the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics browser opt-out</a>.</p>
            <p>The site does not currently change its behavior in response to a browser's Do Not Track signal.</p>

            <h2 class="t-h2">How long we keep information</h2>
            <p>We keep entry records, including email addresses, across tournament seasons to support past results
                and access to your entries. Entries are not automatically deleted at the end of a season.
                You can request deletion. Technical logs, backups, and copies held by service providers may
                remain for their applicable retention periods.</p>

            <h2 class="t-h2">Questions, corrections, or deletion</h2>
            <p>Contact the Bracket 10 organizer who invited you to play to ask about this notice or request
                access, correction, or deletion of your information. Include your entry name and tournament year.
                We may need to verify that the entry belongs to you before making changes.</p>

            <h2 class="t-h2">Changes to this notice</h2>
            <p>We will update this page and its date when our practices change.</p>
            <a href="/">Back to Bracket 10</a>
        </main>
    </div>
    <%- include('partials/rulesModal') %>
    <%- include('partials/scripts') %>
</body>

</html>
